A||||2||deceler8||Are all 2.5 rocker covers alike ?||||1
Z||000000||deceler8||09-15-1999||07:44 PM||||I just purchased a 1986 2m4 and I love it to death. Couldn't afford one when they were new...not a problem now.<P>My question is...The rocker arm cover leaks oil, and appears to be bent enough that I'd like to just get another one. Is the rocker arm cover the same on all 2.5 liter engines for the '86 model year, and what covers will fit this '86 2.5 liter engine ?<P>Thanks in advance for the info.||||reg||1
Z||000001||David||09-15-1999||09:05 PM||||I've put a valve cover from a balancer shaft engine, an '88 Olds I think, on to my '86 Fiero and they appear to be the same.  There is an aluminum cover made by Edelbrock or Holley or someone that looks good in the picture.  Looks like it won't get bent up every time that the cover is removed.  This is probably how I will go the next time that I have to remove my valve cover.||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||09-17-1999||10:22 AM||||Thanks David...Got a good, straight cover at a junkyard off a smashed Celebrity...$5.<P>Painted it up, put it on...doesn't leak.<P>Great forum here.||||reg||1
